tes:", "url": "https://wikipedia2007.classicistranieri.com/s/t/r/Striptease_%28film%29.html"}]}, "The 1996 film *Striptease* is an adaptation of Carl Hiaasen's 1993 novel *Strip Tease*. Andrew Bergman wrote and directed it, and it starred Demi Moore, Armand Assante, Ving Rhames, Robert Patrick, and Burt Reynolds Striptease is a 1996 American black comedy film written, co-produced and directed by Andrew Bergman. The story follows a former FBI employee who turns to stripping and gets pulled into a custody fight and a corruption plot.\n\nSources disagree on some details. Wikipedia lists the budget as $50 million, while a fandom wiki gives $40 million. Wikipedia names Columbia Pictures as distributor, but another wiki credits Warner Bros. Pictures. Critics panned the film, and it won several Razzies, including Worst Picture of 1996 Striptease was generally not well-received by critics. The film wound up winning several Golden Raspberry Awards (Razzies)."], "durationSeconds": 5.822393458999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_016pcG2GAZWhWQpRdzfpy76y", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
